# Linear epic

## How to use

Create or update a project with `save_project`. An epic is not an issue. A milestone is a phase inside this project; create one with `save_milestone` only when the user asks for phases.

- `name`: the epic title.
- `summary`: one sentence, at most 255 characters. Use the Summary line below.
- `description`: the body below, without the Summary line.
- `addTeams` or `setTeams`: team name or id from `list_teams`.
- `priority`: `1` Urgent, `2` High, `3` Medium, or `4` Low. Use `3` unless the user states otherwise.
- `addInitiatives`: only an initiative the user names. This MCP cannot create one.

Stories, bugs, features, and improvements under this epic are issues. Set their `project` to this project's name, id, or `P-ENG-123` after the project exists.

## Body

```markdown
## Outcome

[Who this epic serves, and what is true when it is done.]

## In scope

- [Capability or problem this project includes.]
- [Capability or problem this project includes.]

## Out of scope

- [Work this project does not include.]

## Success criteria

- [ ] [Observable outcome.]
- [ ] [Observable outcome.]
```
